00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:29.120
I like when Barney said, guess who nailed the chick from Metro News 1 last night.
我喜欢巴尼说的那句，猜猜昨晚谁把《都市新闻1台》的辣妹给睡了。

313
00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.820
I like that she grudgingly high-fives him.
我喜欢罗宾很不情愿地跟他击掌。

314
00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:31.500
She's like, it's true.
她好像在说，确实如此。

315
00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.340
If we're going back to normal, I have to high-five him about this chick he nailed.
如果我们要恢复正常，我必须为他睡了这个辣妹跟他击掌。

316
00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:36.060
Yeah.
对。

317
00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:37.480
It's very funny.
这非常搞笑。

318
00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:44.940
There's a, you know, when these roles change and flip and morph, there's this, I don't know,
有种，你知道的，当这些角色转变、翻转和变形时，有种，我不知道，

319
00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:50.180
we're always trying to, like, move chess pieces forward and keep things the same, all at the same time.
我们总是试图，一边推进棋子，一边又让一切保持原样，两手都要抓。

320
00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.160
That is the, what a great way to put it.
这就是，这个说法太棒了。

321
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.380
That is the exact art of a nine-season show.
这正是九季长剧的精妙艺术所在。

322
00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.160
It's exactly what we're trying to do.
这正是我们一直在努力做的事。

323
00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:57.720
Yeah.
对。

324
00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.160
But I mean them as characters.
但我是指他们作为角色而言。

325
00:12:59.540 --> 00:12:59.800
Yeah.
对。

326
00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:00.400
That's what I mean.
我就是这个意思。

327
00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:07.160
Like, you're trying to find new speeds and also be somebody's comfort show and not fuck it up too much.
就像，你既要寻找新的节奏，又要成为某人的治愈系剧集，还不能搞砸得太厉害。

328
00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.400
And still create ways for them to all hang out in the bar.
还要创造各种让他们能一起在酒吧闲逛的方式。

329
00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:20.820
But if you think about Ted's anger or fury, rather, at Barney, like, is, there's a, there's a, I mean, it's kind of biblical.
但如果你想想泰德对巴尼的愤怒或狂怒，简直，有种，怎么说呢，有点像圣经里的桥段。

330
00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.340
Like, it's funny we're talking about Cain and Abel, but, like, there's a banishment.
就像，我们讨论该隐和亚伯很有趣，但，有种放逐的感觉。

331
00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:24.280
There's exile.
那是流放。

332
00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:24.840
It is death.
那就是死亡。

333
00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.700
He's exiled from the booth.
他被逐出了卡座。

334
00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.680
He broke a commandment and he's exiled to the desert.
他违反了诫命，被流放到了沙漠。

335
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.580
And they're his commandments.
而且那些还是他自己定下的诫命。

336
00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.740
They're his commandments, which is even worse.
那是他自己的诫命，这就更糟了。

337
00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:36.760
And it's, in some ways, he taught Ted too well, because Ted is like.
而且从某种程度上说，他把泰德教得太好了，因为泰德就像是。

338
00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:37.520
Yeah.
对。

339
00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.720
I know the gravity of your rules.
我知道你的规则有多严重。

340
00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:45.020
I like, yeah, I like that line from Ted, which he performed really well, which, which was, I thought I was the limit.
我喜欢，对，我喜欢泰德的那句台词，他演得真好，那就是，我以为我是底线。

341
00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:49.620
I thought I was the one thing you would have integrity about.
我以为我是你唯一会坚守原则的事物。

342
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:54.640
And he is more angry at Barney than Robin for this, for that reason.
因为这个原因，他生巴尼的气比生罗宾的气还要大。

343
00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:55.460
And that's interesting.
这很有意思。

344
00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.620
It's a little crazy, but I get it.
这有点疯狂，但我能理解。

345
00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:58.280
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

346
00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.880
I mean, I understand why that's true.
我是说，我明白为什么会这样。

347
00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:05.860
And I think that Ted is right to be hurt and Barney knows it.
而且我认为泰德感到受伤是合情合理的，巴尼也心知肚明。

348
00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:06.660
Yeah.
对。

349
00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:07.180
You know?
你知道吗？

350
00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:07.860
Yeah.
对。

351
00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.620
I really, I think that limo scene is actually very deep.
我真的，我觉得那场加长轿车戏其实非常有深度。

352
00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:15.520
And Barney being left alone in that limo at the end is really sad.
而且最后巴尼一个人被留在加长轿车里真的好难过。

353
00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:16.240
Yeah.
对。

354
00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:24.680
And it's, the other thing is, I love the, the, the, the court case of this, the court case that Marshall is hired to litigate, out of work lawyer Marshall,
还有就是，另一个点是，我喜欢，我喜欢马歇尔接手的那个案子，那个失业律师马歇尔受雇去打官司的案子，

355
00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.400
who has lost his job by yelling at artillery Arthur.
他因为对炮兵亚瑟大吼大叫而丢了工作。

356
00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:35.300
He, he, I love that he's put to work parsing the law of the bro code and that he has, he has to be honeSt.
他，他，我喜欢他被安排去剖析兄弟法则的法律条文，而且他必须诚实。

357
00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.100
He's, he's taking it seriously enough to be honeSt.
他，他对待这件事很认真，力求诚实。

358
00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.640
And he's like, no, no, I cannot find Ted.
他就好像在说，不，不，我找不到泰德。

359
00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:40.280
I don't know.
我不知道。

360
00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.740
This is airtight.
这毫无破绽。

361
00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:42.720
Ted is airtight.
泰德天衣无缝。

362
00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.120
Ted has been a bro to you, Barney.
泰德对你一直很够兄弟，巴尼。

363
00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:45.640
Yeah.
对。

364
00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:51.700
And the instances that we see of Ted upholding the bro code was one of my favorite little vignettes within this episode.
我们看到的泰德捍卫兄弟法则的那些片段，是我在这集里最喜欢的小插曲之一。

365
00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:57.480
The little grabber thing, handing up condoms to him and then taking the money to go by.
那个小抓手，递避孕套给他，然后拿钱去买东西。

366
00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.220
That's a scene Ted doesn't even appear in, but it's hilarious.
那是泰德甚至都没有出场的戏，但太搞笑了。

367
00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.100
You know, it's so funny.
你知道，太好笑了。

368
00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:04.920
I was, I was watching that and I was like, I don't remember shooting this.
我当时在看，心想，我不记得拍过这个。

369
00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.520
And then I was like, I definitely wasn't the given hand.
然后我想，那绝对不是我的手。

370
00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:10.860
That was like, that was probably Dave Baker in props.
那大概是道具师戴夫·贝克。

371
00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:12.320
But it's funny.
但很好笑。

372
00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.900
Like when you're like, I have no memory of this.
就像当你觉得，我对这个毫无印象。

373
00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.920
And I'm like, yeah, I know that was supposed to be me, but I was long gone.
我想，对，我知道那本来该是我，但我早就走了。

374
00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:17.440
I was home.
我回家了。

375
00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:17.940
I was at home.
我在家里。

376
00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:22.800
Because when would you, being crouched outside that window with a little grabber claw hand?
因为你什么时候会蹲在那个窗户外面，手里拿着一个小抓手爪？

377
00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:23.560
You would have remembered that.
你肯定会记得的。

378
00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:23.900
No, I didn't.
不，我没有。

379
00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.000
That wasn't my hand.
那不是我的手。

380
00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:27.860
Sorry for the folks at home, but that wasn't, that wasn't my hand.
对不起电视机前的观众，但那不是，那真的不是我的手。

381
00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:28.640
Sorry to destroy the illusion.
抱歉打破了幻觉。

382
00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.120
The close observers who understand what my hand looks like.
那些知道我的手长什么样子的细心观察者。

383
00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.740
Dave Baker really performed that grabber.
戴夫·贝克真的把那个抓手演活了。

384
00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:35.860
I think very, I felt like Ted, you know what I mean?
我觉得，我感觉就像泰德，你知道我的意思吗？

385
00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:36.560
It felt like Ted.
感觉很像泰德。

386
00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:43.020
And also, what was the one where he had to, he had to like really say something he didn't want to say?
还有，还有一个是什么，就是他必须，他必须说出一些他真的不想说的话？

387
00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.440
And he had to say, it was a Russian.
他不得不说，那是一个俄罗斯人。

388
00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:46.300
He had to say da.
他不得不说“达”。

389
00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:50.140
Yes, ending all these horrible things that had the board.
没错，对委员会那些可怕的事情全都表示赞同。

390
00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:53.960
No, there was nothing about those parts of the lie that got Barney laid.
不，谎言中那些能让巴尼泡到妞的部分根本没什么关系。

391
00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:59.600
It was just Barney throwing Ted into the bus and Ted still yes, ending it or da, ending it in Russian.
那只是巴尼把泰德推给汽车当替死鬼，而泰德仍然对它表示赞同，或者用俄语说“达”。

392
00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:06.720
And you love Ted through that whole montage, and it's driving Barney mad.
在整段蒙太奇中，你会越来越爱泰德，而这快要把巴尼逼疯了。

393
00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:15.060
Barney needs a loophole because this is Barney's way of processing his guilt, and he knows deep down he's not going to find that loophole because he fucked up.
巴尼需要一个漏洞，因为这是巴尼消化负罪感的方式，而且他内心深处知道自己找不到这个漏洞，因为他搞砸了。

394
00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:15.700
He broke the broken.
他打破了禁忌。

395
00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:26.500
But he also, like, there's a real revelation of, and we already knew this, like, Barney's fidelity to Ted and the bro kind of friendship,
但他也，就像，有一个真正的揭示，我们之前就知道了，比如，巴尼对泰德的忠诚以及兄弟情谊，

396
00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:32.720
their kind of Butch Cassidy Sundance kid kind of mythology he's built up in his head around the two of them.
那种他在脑海中为两人构建的类似《虎豹小霸王》的神话色彩。

397
00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:37.760
It's way more important to him than any woman, than any sex.
这对他来说比任何女人、任何性爱都重要得多。

398
00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:45.200
Like, it's almost like getting women is a pretext for hanging and having these crazy stories.
就像，泡妞几乎成了聚会和经历这些疯狂故事的借口。

399
00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.600
Like, it's not the end goal.
这并不是最终目标。

400
00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:51.480
The goal is a great memorable night where crazy stuff happens.
目标是一个充满疯狂事情的、令人难忘的美妙夜晚。

401
00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.020
Yeah, I think that's it.
对，我想就是这样。

402
00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.980
It's the activity they can do together.
这是他们能一起进行的活动。

403
00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.120
Some people might be basketball.
对有些人来说可能是打篮球。

404
00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:59.080
Some people might be going fishing.
对有些人来说可能是去钓鱼。

405
00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.000
This is what it is for Barney.
这就是巴尼的方式。

406
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:07.120
And it's mostly not about actually catching the fish, as it were, because you mostly don't catch the fish.
而且这基本上不是为了真的去钓鱼，可以说是这样，因为你大部分时候根本钓不到鱼。

407
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:11.980
I think Barney's numbers being what they are, I think it's mostly about being with your bro.
我觉得以巴尼的战绩来看，我觉得这主要是为了和你的好兄弟在一起。

408
00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.740
And I think it's Barney's most important relationship in life is Ted.
而且我认为巴尼生命中最最重要的关系就是泰德。

409
00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:16.420
Yeah.
对。

410
00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.620
And this is the episode where he loses that.
这就是他失去这种关系的那集。

411
00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:19.480
Yeah.
对。

412
00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:20.220
And I think—
而且我觉得——

413
00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.280
And he really feels unmoored.
而且他真的感到心神不定。

414
00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:35.280
You can really see in Neil's eyes, like, I don't know who I am when not in relation to this person, this group of people, this bar, this booth, this England.
你真的能在尼尔的眼神中看到，就像是，我不知道当我不与这个人、这群人、这个酒吧、这个卡座、这片英格兰产生联系时，我是谁。

415
00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:36.160
Yeah.
对。

416
00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:36.840
I'm quoting Shakespeare now.
我现在是在引用莎士比亚的话。

417
00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:37.280
This England.
这片英格兰。

418
00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:48.280
I really like how—yeah, and Barney, it's funny that you're getting sort of Shakespearean about it, because, like, Barney feels like a tragic character.
我真的很喜欢——对，而且巴尼，你对此变得有点莎士比亚式真搞笑，因为，就像是，巴尼感觉像个悲剧人物。

419
00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:53.260
He feels like this haunted, like, Macbeth, like, out-damn-spot kind of thing.
他感觉像个受折磨的人，就像麦克白那样，带着“滚开，该死的血迹”那种感觉。

420
00:17:53.260 --> 00:18:04.680
Like, he's—he—when he is trying to find his way out of this, and he's saying, I'm, you know, sublimating my anxiety by buying things out of the SkyMall catalog.
就像他——他——当他试图摆脱这种状态时，他说，你知道的，我在通过在SkyMall目录上买东西来转移我的焦虑。

421
00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:07.180
He's, like, binging on buying, overbuying.
他就像是，疯狂购物，过度消费。

422
00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:12.940
He's like—I love that line where he's like, I have, you know, seven self-cleaning litter boxes, and I don't even have a kid.
他就像——我好喜欢他说的这句台词，他说，你知道的，我有七个自动清洁猫砂盆，而我甚至连个孩子都没有。

423
00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.720
That's an insane line.
那是句疯狂的台词。

424
00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:17.440
That is a great Stephen Lloyd joke.
那绝对是个棒极了的斯蒂芬·劳埃德式笑话。

425
00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:24.820
That is—I gotta give—that is a kind of—when we talk about a Stephen Lloyd joke, like, very dark, very weird, and it's only a joke in the last word.
那是——我得承认——那是一种——当我们说起斯蒂芬·劳埃德式的笑话时，非常黑暗，非常古怪，而且直到最后一个词才抖出包袱。

426
00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:25.620
Right.
没错。

427
00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.860
You replace cat with kid, and it's genius.
你把猫换成孩子，这就是天才。

428
00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:28.800
It's weird.
这太怪了。

429
00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:29.960
It's definitely weird.
这绝对很怪。

430
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.760
A lesser writer might have had cat in there.
水平逊色一点的编剧可能会直接写猫了。

431
00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.600
I might have been like, oh, it's funny.
我当时可能会觉得，哦，这挺搞笑的。

432
00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.280
He's buying these silly things, and that's it.
他买这些傻里傻气的东西，就这就完了。

433
00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.240
The Stephen Lloyd twist of making it kid.
斯蒂芬·劳埃德的妙笔在于把它改成了孩子。

434
00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:41.620
Wait, you—you think that's what parenthood is?
等等，你——你觉得为人父母就是这样的吗？

435
00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.280
It's so dark and weird.
这太黑暗太诡异了。

436
00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.820
So I gotta give Stephen a big shout-out.
所以我得向斯蒂芬致以巨大的敬意。

437
00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:57.740
Well, it's also like Barney—in Scorpion and the Toad, his scorpion nature is at play and is not something he can control.
嗯，这也像是巴尼——在《蝎子与青蛙》里，他蝎子的本性在作祟，而且这不是他能控制的。

438
00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.620
It's bigger than him.
这超出了他的掌控。

439
00:18:58.680 --> 00:18:59.640
It's just his nature.
这就是他的本性。

440
00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:00.380
It's his nature.
这就是他的本性。

441
00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:08.820
But it's Marshall, and it's lighter, even though he's like a jerk, and you get angry at him, and he gets a great comeuppance in that episode.
但那是马修，而且氛围更轻松，尽管他就像个混蛋，你会生他的气，而且他在那一集里得到了应有的报应。

442
00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:09.280
He does.
他确实得到了。

443
00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:12.180
But in this one, it's also his scorpion nature.
但在这一家里，这也体现了他的蝎子本性。

444
00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:12.820
Yeah.
对。

445
00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:25.460
That even though you guys have layered it in really beautifully of watching him and Robin kind of just enjoy each other and legitimately become friends.
尽管你们把这一点层层铺垫得非常美妙，看着他和罗宾享受彼此的陪伴，并且顺理成章地成为了朋友。

446
00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:33.800
And him, I think what you see, what at least I'm noticing, is that Barney has so little respect for women, and in fact,
而且他，我觉得你所看到的，至少我所注意到的是，巴尼对女性缺乏尊重，事实上，

447
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.980
the women he sleeps with are women that he simply doesn't respect or disregards.
他与之发生关系的女性都是那些他根本不尊重或是不放在眼里的女性。

448
00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:39.840
He doesn't grant them full personhood.
他没有赋予她们作为一个完整人类的尊严。

449
00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:40.440
Yes.
没错。

450
00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:44.640
And it seems that the more he gets to know Robin, he's like, wait a minute.
而且似乎随着他对罗宾越来越了解，他心里想：等等。

451
00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:54.620
Like, this person is cool, beautiful, fun, smart, can hang, gets my jokes, you know, can match me scotch for scotch.
就好像，这个人很酷、很美、很有趣、很聪明，玩得开，能接住我的梗，你知道的，能陪我一杯接一杯地喝苏格兰威士忌。

452
00:19:54.620 --> 00:20:07.000
Like, there's just something about her that I think is, she's becoming very dimensional to him, and thus very attractive to him in a way that I don't think he is comfortable with,
就是，她身上某种特质让他觉得，在她身上展现出了很多维度的魅力，因此对他产生了极大的吸引力，而这种吸引力以一种某种程度上他并不习惯的方式存在着，

453
00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.360
necessarily, with women being.
或者说，不习惯女性拥有这种魅力。

454
00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:13.680
Because it gives, the power imbalance gets corrected.
因为这使得权力失衡得到了纠正。

455
00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:14.320
Yeah.
没错。

456
00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:16.040
And Barney wants to have the power.
而巴尼想要掌握主动权。

457
00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.680
He wants to have the power to seduce.
他想要拥有诱惑的权力。

458
00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:18.780
He wants to have the power to leave.
他想要拥有随时抽身的权力。

459
00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:20.220
Yeah, I think so.
对，我也这么觉得。

460
00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:25.760
And I think that's why neither Robin or Barney even considers turning this into a real relationship right away,
所以我觉得这也是为什么罗宾和巴尼甚至都没有考虑过立刻把这段关系变成真的恋爱，

461
00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.800
because I think they're both scared that there is a real connection there.
因为我觉得他们两个都害怕彼此之间真的产生了某种深厚的连结。

462
00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:36.160
And I've been enjoying, in season three, remembering the little kind of Easter egg hints, the little breadcrumbs we're leaving of this.
而且我一直很享受在第三季中去回味那些隐藏的彩蛋线索，那些我们为这段关系留下的蛛丝马迹。

463
00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:39.140
Even watching The Bracket, which is a couple episodes before this.
甚至在看《黑名单》那集的时候，那是在这集之前的几集。

464
00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.920
We talked to Joe Kelly about that episode.
我们和乔·凯利聊过那一集。

465
00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:48.840
I forgot to bring up this moment when we talked about it, which is, isn't it in The Bracket where Barney whispers to Robin and she laughs?
我们聊的时候我忘了提那个桥段了，就是，是不是在《黑名单》里，巴尼对罗宾耳语然后她笑了？

466
00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:52.540
No, shoot, which I'm getting my episodes confused, where she laughs when she lies.
不对，哎呀，我把集数记混了，是她撒谎时会笑的那集。

467
00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.940
Yeah, yeah, that's The Bracket.
对，对，那是《黑名单》。

468
00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:58.940
And he whispers in her ear and says something very dirty about him.
然后他在她耳边低语，说了一些关于他自己的非常大尺度的黄色废话。

469
00:20:59.160 --> 00:20:59.980
Oh, oh, yeah.
哦，哦，对。

470
00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.980
You know, like something very, like, sexual of nature.
你知道的，就是那种非常、带有性暗示的话。

471
00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:05.760
And she does that nervous laugh, because he's like, you're turned on, aren't you?
然后她发出了那种紧张的笑声，因为他说，你动心了对吧？

472
00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:06.600
She's like, no, I'm not.
她就说，才没有，我才没有。

473
00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:07.680
She does, like, the little laugh.
她就发出了那种小小的笑声。

474
00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:07.960
Yeah.
是啊。

475
00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:15.080
Those were all, we were doing those very intentionally, and there's a bunch of them in season three where you see there's something going on.
这些都是我们非常刻意去安排的，第三季里有很多这样的细节，你能看出他们之间有些不对劲。

476
00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:19.020
There was that great one where she doesn't have makeup on, where she says, I'm not wearing makeup.
还有那个很棒的桥段，她没化妆的时候说，我没化妆。

477
00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:19.300
Yeah.
对。

478
00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:20.860
He says, my God, you're beautiful.
他说，天哪，你真美。

479
00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:21.960
God, you're beautiful.
天哪，你真美。

480
00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:23.980
That's early in season three, I think.
我想那是第三季初期的事。

481
00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:32.400
But I also, if we have Neil, or when we have Neil or Kobe back on, I want to say, what did he whisper to you?
但我也想，如果我们能请到尼尔，或者当尼尔或寇碧再次做客时，我想问问，他当时到底对你耳语了什么？

482
00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:37.540
Because I remember what both of them would whisper to me, and it was not suitable for work.
因为我记得他们两个以前对我说悄悄话的时候，内容都是极其不宜在工作场合播放的。

483
00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.280
Let's just say, not suitable.
这么说吧，完全不宜。

484
00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:44.680
And I'm so curious what he said to her, because also, I think that's in the blooper.
我特别好奇他对她说了什么，因为我觉得那也拍进了花絮里。

485
00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:48.380
Those were always in the bloopers, like, when people would break.
那些内容总是会被收录在花絮里，比如演员笑场的时候。

486
00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:48.940
Yes.
对。

487
00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.120
That is a great question.
这真的是个好问题。

488
00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:55.120
Hold on to that, because I think we are, we will be talking to Kobe again soon.
你把它记着，因为我想我们很快又会和寇碧聊天了。

489
00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.120
So hold on to that one.
所以留着这个问题吧。

490
00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:56.680
That's a good one.
这是个好问题。

491
00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:57.200
All right.
好吧。

492
00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:58.160
I loved, uh.
我喜欢，呃。

493
00:21:58.160 --> 00:22:00.860
Actually, just to make this him, we have already.
其实，为了符合时间线，我们其实已经。

494
00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.500
We will have already done it.
我们其实已经录过了。

495
00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:06.660
You have, in the previous episode, you have probably heard us talking to Kobe.
在上一期节目里，你们可能已经听到我们和寇碧的对话了。

496
00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:09.280
Let's pretend that that happened in the previous episode.
我们就假设那已经在上一期发生过了吧。

497
00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:09.580
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

498
00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.920
And, yes, that was a great talk we had.
而且，是的，那是一次非常棒的对话。

499
00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:17.560
I liked when, uh, when, uh, Kobe says, I'm going to take a shower until June.
我喜欢，呃，当寇碧说“我要去洗个澡，直到六月再出来”的时候。

500
00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:23.000
And Lily's curiosity, too, about, like, what was it like?
还有莉莉也很好奇，当时到底是什么感觉？

501
00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:29.840
That was really, like, just the idea that they're like, well, now that it's happened, you've set foot on the moon.
那感觉真的是……就好像是，他们会觉得，好吧，既然这事已经发生了，你就算是在月球上踏足了。

502
00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:30.600
What is it like?
那种感觉是什么样的？

503
00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:33.460
Like, this is an incredibly exotic, weird thing has happened.
就好像，这发生了一件极其猎奇、诡异的事。

504
00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.320
You've entered that realm with Barney.
你和巴尼一起进入了那个领域。

505
00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:36.560
It's like morbid curiosity.
就像是一种病态的好奇心。

506
00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:37.900
It's like, you've got to tell us.
就好像在说，你必须跟我们讲讲。

507
00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:41.280
Yes, but a little bit turned on, like a little bit into, a little bit too into it.
是的，但还有点儿兴奋，就好像有点儿沉迷，有点儿沉迷过头了。

508
00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:42.000
Yeah.
对。

509
00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:46.520
What if Barney said Stella makes this one look like a filthy bag of garbage?
要是巴尼说斯黛拉跟这比起来就像一袋恶心的垃圾呢？

510
00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:51.420
I think I have to give the writer Steve Healy some credit there.
我觉得我得在那儿给编剧史蒂夫·希利记上一功。

511
00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:53.220
I may have been name-checking Steve Healy there.
我刚才可能顺便提到了史蒂夫·希利的名字。

512
00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:55.340
He would often do a big bag of garbage.
他以前经常会说“一大袋垃圾”。

513
00:22:55.760 --> 00:22:58.660
The blank makes blank look like a big old bag of garbage.
“某某让某某看起来像个老旧的大垃圾袋。”

514
00:22:58.780 --> 00:23:01.900
We were on American Dad together, and he would say that form all the time.
我们以前一起做过《美国老爹》，他总是用这种句式。

515
00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:05.120
And I feel like I might have ripped that off from him and never given him credit.
我觉得我可能从他那里抄袭了这个，却从来没给过他署名或感谢。

516
00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:08.020
Steve Healy wrote one of the funniest books I ever read.
史蒂夫·希利写过我读过的最搞笑的书之一。

517
00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:09.540
How I Became a Famous Novelist?
《我如何成为一名著名的小说家》？

518
00:23:09.640 --> 00:23:10.460
How I Became a Famous NoveliSt.
《我如何成为一名著名的小说家》。

519
00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:11.500
A hilarious book.
一本令人捧腹的书。

520
00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:12.160
Hilarious.
太搞笑了。

521
00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.700
Yes, so I read that book as I was contemplating writing my own book.
是的，所以我正盘算着写自己的书时读了那本书。

522
00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:24.260
And I found it very inspirational because it is a genuinely laugh-out-loud funny novel by a TV comedy.
我发现它极具启发性，因为这是一部由电视喜剧人创作的、真正让人捧腹大笑的小说。

523
00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:27.040
One of the hardest I've laughed in books I've ever read.
这是我读过的书里让我笑得最厉害的之一。

524
00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:31.760
I think I met him one night and told him, but please pass that on.
我想我有一天晚上遇到过他并告诉过他，但请把这话转达给他。

525
00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:36.960
So this book, I'll just give the pitch for it because it's so wonderful.
所以这本书，我来简单介绍一下它的主旨，因为它太精彩了。

526
00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:40.440
It's a guy who's deeply depressed.
讲的是一个深度抑郁的家伙。

527
00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:48.000
His life isn't going anywhere, and he gets an invite, a wedding, save the date for a while away,
他的生活毫无进展，然后他收到了一份邀请，是一个远期婚礼的“预留日期”通知，

528
00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:51.220
to an ex-girlfriend's wedding that he's still kind of friends with.
去参加一个前女友的婚礼，他们现在还算有点朋友关系。

529
00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:59.140
And he decides that he cannot show up to this wedding unless he is a best-selling New York Times best-selling noveliSt.
于是他决定，除非自己成为一名畅销书作家——《纽约时报》畅销书小说家，否则他绝不出席这个婚礼。

530
00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:03.740
So he spends the next whatever year writing this book and getting published.
所以他在接下来的不知哪一年里写了这本书并得以出版。

531
00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:10.800
But he studies the New York Times bestseller list to try to craft a novel that has all the elements of everything that is commercial and stuff.
但他研究了《纽约时报》畅销书排行榜，试图精心构思一部集齐了所有商业元素等等的小说。

532
00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.000
Yeah, he's basically doing AI.
对，他基本上在搞人工智能。

533
00:24:12.260 --> 00:24:13.540
He's a human doing AI.
他是一个搞人工智能的人类。

534
00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:15.140
He's writing an AI novel.
他在写一本AI小说。

535
00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:19.340
So he writes a book about lovers who get parted during World War II.
所以他写了一本关于在二战期间失散的情侣的书。

536
00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:22.080
There's a dog that's in there.
里面还有一只狗。

537
00:24:22.240 --> 00:24:24.220
It's like all the elements of what people...
就好像大家喜欢的所有元素的集合……

538
00:24:24.220 --> 00:24:28.900
And the goal is it's like a road trip movie, too, where they have to scatter someone's ashes into a tornado.
而且目标是它也有点像公路电影，他们必须把某人的骨灰撒进龙卷风里。

539
00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:33.440
So it's like the Tornado Chasers Club or something.
所以这就像是龙卷风追逐者俱乐部什么的。

540
00:24:33.540 --> 00:24:34.160
It's like some of the...
这就像是其中的一些……

541
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:35.680
So it's really funny.
所以真的非常搞笑。

542
00:24:35.820 --> 00:24:42.720
And Josh, I knew I was going to write a novel where I wanted to make similar jokes about books about disability,
乔希，我知道我要写一部小说，我想在里面开一些类似的玩笑，关于残疾的书的玩笑，

543
00:24:42.880 --> 00:24:44.900
jokes about how disability is taught about in pop culture.
关于流行文化中如何看待残疾的玩笑。

544
00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:51.040
And I found how I became a famous novelist to be a really inspiring book.
我发现《我如何成为一名著名的小说家》是一本真正鼓舞人心的书。

545
00:24:51.040 --> 00:24:53.000
I should tell Steve this because I was like,
我应该把这告诉史蒂夫，因为我想过——

546
00:24:53.380 --> 00:24:56.000
I'm going to do some of these same things in my novel.
我要在我的小说里也用上一些这样的小把戏。

547
00:24:56.100 --> 00:25:00.260
I'm going to try to write something that's actually funny and comment on pop culture a little bit.
我要试着写一些真正有趣的东西，并且稍微评论一下流行文化。

548
00:25:00.380 --> 00:25:05.680
And he did it in a way that was genuinely funny, but you felt like there were stakes and you felt invested.
而他做到这一点的方式既真正有趣，又让你觉得有切身利害关系，并让你深陷其中。

549
00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:07.040
It didn't feel like a parody book.
它感觉不像是一本恶搞书。

550
00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:07.820
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

551
00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:08.200
It still was a...
它依然是个……

552
00:25:08.200 --> 00:25:09.080
But you were invested in the characters.
但你对这些角色投入了真感情。

553
00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:11.000
It's like a proper novel on its own merits.
它本身就像一部正儿八经的小说。

554
00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:11.320
It's a novel, yeah.
对，它就是部小说。

555
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:12.100
It's a proper novel.
一部真正的小说。

556
00:25:12.100 --> 00:25:15.440
It also really pokes fun at the publishing industry and the...
它还狠狠地讽刺了出版业，以及……

557
00:25:15.440 --> 00:25:20.420
Yeah, and I knew I was going to do that for Hollywood a little bit in my book and how disability is portrayed sometimes in Hollywood.
对，我知道我的书里也会稍微讽刺一下好莱坞，以及好莱坞有时是如何刻画残疾人群体的。

558
00:25:20.920 --> 00:25:30.940
And I thought Steve did a brilliant parody of just the ridiculousness of the industry of trying to create a best-selling book.
我觉得史蒂夫对那种为了炮制畅销书而产生行业荒诞象的讽刺简直绝了。

559
00:25:31.100 --> 00:25:32.940
Not write a good book, but create a best-selling book.
不是写一本好书，而是炮制一本畅销书。

560
00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:34.180
The book industry, a big pile of garbage.
图书出版业，简直一大堆垃圾。

561
00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:39.160
You know, and that was that big bag of garbage.
你知道的，那可真是一大包垃圾。

562
00:25:39.160 --> 00:25:41.600
I think that was my little Steve Healy shout-out without...
我觉得那就是我对史蒂夫·希利的小小致敬，没有……

563
00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:41.650
Oh, that's nice.
噢，那挺好的。

564
00:25:41.650 --> 00:25:42.480
I wonder if he ever knew.
我在想他知不知道。

565
00:25:42.620 --> 00:25:45.740
So I'm glad we're saying it now and we complimented his novel.
所以我很高兴我们现在把它说出来，还称赞了他的小说。

566
00:25:45.880 --> 00:25:47.840
Now I feel like I've karmically made...
现在我觉得我从因果报应上……

567
00:25:47.840 --> 00:25:49.520
Upheld the bro code to Steve Healy.
对史蒂夫·希利恪守了兄弟信条。

568
00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:53.620
You know what I...
你知道我……

569
00:25:53.620 --> 00:25:56.200
I mean, one of my favorite just set pieces.
我是说，我最喜欢的布景之一。

570
00:25:56.520 --> 00:26:00.700
Like, I love old-timey flashbacks on the show to, like, ancient Greece.
比如，我喜欢剧中的那种古早闪回，比如去到古希腊。

571
00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:02.200
That was a very funny...
那真是非常搞笑的……

572
00:26:02.200 --> 00:26:05.200
And by the way, beautiful costumes, beautiful set.
顺便说一句，服装很美，布景也很美。

573
00:26:05.380 --> 00:26:06.240
It looked great.
看起来真棒。

574
00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:08.960
Kelly Harris as a bar wench.
凯莉·哈里斯饰演一个酒吧女招待。

575
00:26:11.040 --> 00:26:14.420
Kelly worked in production in a bunch of different roles and was on the show many years.
凯莉在制作组干过各种不同的职务，在这部剧里待了很多年。

576
00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:18.200
And that's Kelly that is, you know, under Barney's arm at...
那就是凯莉，你知道的，在巴尼的胳膊……

577
00:26:18.660 --> 00:26:20.320
Barnabas's arm at the bar there.
在酒吧里巴纳巴斯的胳膊下。

578
00:26:20.420 --> 00:26:20.920
It's really fun.
真的很有趣。

579
00:26:20.980 --> 00:26:22.360
I love when George Washington says,
我特别喜欢乔治·华盛顿说的那句，

580
00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:24.480
I have to get back to me, D.C.
我得回我的哥伦比亚特区去了。

581
00:26:24.800 --> 00:26:25.640
Me, D.C.
我的哥伦比亚特区。

582
00:26:26.160 --> 00:26:32.020
I love that it was totally clear that two of the founding fathers had had a Devil's Three-Way together.
我喜欢这种完全毫不掩饰的暗示，两个国父曾经一起搞过双飞。

583
00:26:33.260 --> 00:26:34.420
The Devil's Three-Way.
双飞。

584
00:26:34.460 --> 00:26:35.600
They had a Devil's Three-Way.
他们搞过双飞。

585
00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:37.220
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

586
00:26:37.540 --> 00:26:43.220
And also, like, the fact that it comes back in that flashback among the founding fathers.
而且还有，这事居然在国父们的闪回里再次呼应了。

587
00:26:43.720 --> 00:26:47.860
It's like, it's almost like great, like, delightful heresy.
就感觉，这简直就像是一种绝妙的、令人愉悦的异端邪说。

588
00:26:48.080 --> 00:26:48.540
Yeah.
对。

589
00:26:48.800 --> 00:26:49.800
Like, to say that.
就好像，说出这种话。

590
00:26:50.060 --> 00:26:50.960
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吗？

591
00:26:50.960 --> 00:26:51.780
Yes, absolutely.
是的，完全同意。

592
00:26:52.180 --> 00:26:53.280
And somehow it gives...
而且不知怎么的，它赋予了……

593
00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:56.500
Even though it's absurd, it does weirdly give gravitas to it.
尽管它很荒谬，但它确实离奇地赋予了一种庄严感。

594
00:26:56.580 --> 00:26:58.160
Like, it's a historical time.
就像，这是一个历史时期。

595
00:26:58.280 --> 00:26:59.100
We're thinking about the Bible.
我们在想着《圣经》。

596
00:26:59.220 --> 00:27:00.060
We're thinking about the Constitution.
我们在想着《宪法》。

597
00:27:00.300 --> 00:27:04.140
Like, big things are being invoked in this episode to give it this weight.
就像，这一集里唤起了很多宏大的事物来赋予它这种分量。

598
00:27:04.160 --> 00:27:05.800
And I feel like it actually works.
我觉得它确实起作用了。

599
00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:08.600
That Bro Code Bible feels significant.
那本《兄弟信条圣经》感觉很有分量。

600
00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:09.860
And, like, it contains gravitas.
而且，它蕴含着庄严感。

601
00:27:09.860 --> 00:27:10.740
It feels hefty.
感觉挺厚重的。

602
00:27:10.740 --> 00:27:12.080
It feels like sacred literature.
感觉就像什么神圣的文学经典。

603
00:27:12.360 --> 00:27:13.340
It really does.
确实如此。

604
00:27:13.600 --> 00:27:13.940
Yeah.
对啊。

605
00:27:13.940 --> 00:27:14.460
It really does.
真的挺像的。

606
00:27:23.280 --> 00:27:28.340
Who, at that point, I think may still have been a writer's assistant and was just great.
当时他好像还是个编剧助理，而且表现得非常棒。

607
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:32.440
And he wrote Barney's blog for every episode of the series.
剧集里每一集的巴尼博客都是他写的。

608
00:27:33.100 --> 00:27:36.260
And we said, you know the voice of Barney so well.
然后我们就说，你对巴尼的语气太熟悉了。

609
00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:38.360
Do you want to head this up as a book?
你想不想牵头把它做成一本书？

610
00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:39.840
I'm losing my chronology.
我的时间线有点混乱了。

611
00:27:39.980 --> 00:27:41.420
Alec, maybe you can see, was Matt a writer yet?
亚历克，也许你能看看，马特当时已经是编剧了吗？

612
00:27:41.420 --> 00:27:42.560
But at this point, I'm completely...
但到这个时候，我完全……

613
00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:43.260
See, I'm being 50.
你看，我这五十岁的人了。

614
00:27:43.600 --> 00:27:45.280
You know, I'm doing future Ted here.
你知道的，我在这儿扮演未来的泰德。

615
00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:52.220
But Matt wrote this book of the Bro Code that, you know, we all pitched some stuff, but it was really Matt.
但马特写了这本《兄弟守则》，你知道，我们大家也贡献了一些内容，但主要还是马特写的。

616
00:27:52.620 --> 00:27:55.480
And that book became a New York Times bestseller.
然后那本书成了《纽约时报》畅销书。

617
00:27:55.680 --> 00:28:00.080
Speaking of bestsellers, like, actually a New York Times bestseller in the comedy category.
说到畅销书，确实是《纽约时报》喜剧类畅销书。

618
00:28:00.900 --> 00:28:03.580
And there were several spinoff books that came from that.
由此还衍生出了好几本书。

619
00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:06.140
But it was, it literally was a bestselling book.
但这绝对是一本畅销书。

620
00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:08.380
I've signed many a Bro Code over the years.
这些年来我签过不少本《兄弟守则》呢。

621
00:28:08.460 --> 00:28:09.540
Yeah, yeah, I bet.
对，对，我敢说肯定不少。

622
00:28:09.840 --> 00:28:10.980
And they're available.
而且现在还能买到。

623
00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:13.680
If people don't know this, I will give it a little plug.
如果大家还不知道的话，我顺便宣传一下。

624
00:28:14.280 --> 00:28:16.020
You can very much go by the Bro Code.
你们完全可以去买《兄弟守则》。

625
00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:17.400
It's a great little bathroom book.
这是一本很棒的厕所读物。

626
00:28:17.580 --> 00:28:19.320
It's not that huge tome.
它不是那种巨大的大部头。

627
00:28:19.440 --> 00:28:20.880
It's not like a big leather mount thing.
也不是那种做成皮面精装的大物件。

628
00:28:21.140 --> 00:28:22.480
It's just like, it's kind of...
它就是那种……

629
00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:23.760
You should do like...
你应该做成像……

630
00:28:23.760 --> 00:28:24.240
It's the Deep Thoughts books.
就像杰克·汉迪的《深思集》那样。

631
00:28:24.320 --> 00:28:27.360
You know, it's basically the Deep Thoughts books, which to me is the highest literature.
你知道，基本上就是《深思集》那样的书，在我看来这就是最高文学。

632
00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:32.280
You should do some sort of, like, anniversary edition of the Bro Code and actually do it in the binding.
你们应该出个什么周年纪念版的《兄弟守则》，而且真的用那种装帧。

633
00:28:32.720 --> 00:28:34.960
Yeah, like the bound kind of sacred copy.
对，就像那种精装的神圣副本。

634
00:28:34.960 --> 00:28:36.360
It weighs 25 pounds.
重达25磅的那种。

635
00:28:36.580 --> 00:28:38.360
Yeah, that would be amazing.
对，那太棒了。

636
00:28:38.620 --> 00:28:39.400
That would be amazing.
那真的太棒了。

637
00:28:39.580 --> 00:28:40.200
We should do that.
我们应该搞一个。

638
00:28:40.580 --> 00:28:40.800
All right.
好吧。

639
00:28:41.080 --> 00:28:41.680
Note to selves.
备忘一下。

640
00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:42.560
We'll tell 20th.
我们跟二十世纪福斯说一声。

641
00:28:44.100 --> 00:28:49.240
I loved when Barney said, technically, you'll be paid by a toy factory in Pyongyang.
我最喜欢巴尼说的那句，从技术上讲，你的薪水是由平壤的一家玩具厂支付的。

642
00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:51.920
What does this guy do for a living?
这家伙到底是干什么工作的？

643
00:28:51.920 --> 00:28:52.700
Is this with the Shredder?
这跟碎纸机有关吗？

644
00:28:52.800 --> 00:28:53.700
This is with the Shredder, right?
这其实跟碎纸机有关吧？

645
00:28:53.820 --> 00:28:54.400
Yeah, the Shredder.
对，碎纸机。

646
00:28:54.480 --> 00:28:56.200
He shreds a phone at one point.
他有一场戏把手机给碎了。

647
00:28:57.300 --> 00:28:58.880
He puts so many things through the Shredder.
他把好多东西都塞进碎纸机里了。

648
00:28:59.020 --> 00:29:00.400
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

649
00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:02.920
Like, you guys gave juSt...
就好像你们只给……

650
00:29:02.920 --> 00:29:05.880
It was like just enough to be like, what does he do?
给得刚好让人忍不住想：他到底是干什么的？

651
00:29:05.880 --> 00:29:08.780
It's like entirely a criminal enterprise.
这完全就像是一个犯罪集团。

652
00:29:09.220 --> 00:29:11.300
Like, there's nothing ethical that he's doing.
可以说，他做的事没有一件是道德的。

653
00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:11.760
Yeah.
没错。

654
00:29:11.880 --> 00:29:12.920
He does it all happily.
而且他干得兴高采烈。

655
00:29:13.320 --> 00:29:13.540
Yeah.
是啊。

656
00:29:13.620 --> 00:29:14.580
But he covers his tracks.
但他把尾巴擦得很干净。

657
00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:15.560
Yes.
是的。

658
00:29:15.940 --> 00:29:16.060
Yes.
没错。

659
00:29:16.280 --> 00:29:16.360
You know?
你知道吗？

660
00:29:16.540 --> 00:29:17.020
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

661
00:29:17.240 --> 00:29:18.040
And it's a series.
而且这是一个系列连载。

662
00:29:18.180 --> 00:29:21.140
It's yet another running mystery in this larger mystery.
这是这个宏大谜团中的又一个连环谜题。

663
00:29:21.140 --> 00:29:21.980
What does Barney do?
巴尼到底是做什么的？

664
00:29:22.100 --> 00:29:24.300
And we do pay it off at the end of the series.
我们在剧集结尾时确实给出了交代。

665
00:29:24.300 --> 00:29:26.240
We tell you what his role was.
我们会告诉你他的角色是什么。

666
00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:28.220
And we see Shredder fallout from it.
我们还会看到由此引发的施耐德余波。

667
00:29:28.480 --> 00:29:29.240
Ooh, we'll get there.
噢，我们等下会聊到。

668
00:29:29.600 --> 00:29:30.020
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

669
00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:31.040
Do you remember this?
你还记得这个吗？

670
00:29:31.080 --> 00:29:31.920
It remains a mystery to me.
对我来说这依然是个谜。

671
00:29:32.040 --> 00:29:33.140
Let's see if this jogs your memory.
我们来看看这能不能唤醒你的记忆。

672
00:29:33.260 --> 00:29:33.600
Yeah, we are.
对，我们会的。

673
00:29:33.820 --> 00:29:37.860
We try not to do too many jump-aheads and spoilers just to keep it about the episode.
我们尽量不做太多跳跃和剧透，好让内容集中在单集本身。

674
00:29:38.060 --> 00:29:39.880
We fail at that consistently.
不过我们在这方面一向做得挺失败的。

675
00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:40.940
But I'll say this.
但我得这么说。

676
00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:42.080
Does this ring any bell for you?
这能让你想起什么吗？

677
00:29:42.340 --> 00:29:45.640
Every time through the series where someone says to Barney, what do you do?
在整部剧中，每次有人问巴尼，你是做什么的？

678
00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:46.480
And he goes, please.
然后他就会说，拜托。

679
00:29:46.660 --> 00:29:46.820
Please.
拜托。

680
00:29:47.160 --> 00:29:50.840
Well, please turns out to be an acronym for what he does.
好吧，“拜托”原来是他工作内容的缩写。

681
00:29:51.140 --> 00:29:52.680
P-L-E-A-S-E.
P-L-E-A-S-E。

682
00:29:52.820 --> 00:29:53.100
Okay.
好吧。

683
00:29:53.440 --> 00:29:53.680
Okay.
行吧。

684
00:29:54.320 --> 00:29:55.020
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

685
00:29:55.940 --> 00:29:56.880
Should we say it to you?
我们要现在告诉你吗？

686
00:29:56.880 --> 00:29:57.720
I only read my lines.
我只读我自己的台词。

687
00:30:02.760 --> 00:30:03.780
Can I ask a question?
我能问个问题吗？

688
00:30:03.940 --> 00:30:11.300
I have a question about the decision to partner Barney and Robin.
关于让巴尼和罗宾凑成一对的这个决定，我有个问题。

689
00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:16.980
Just as writers with the long-running series where you have this beloved Ted and Robin,
作为一部长寿剧的编剧，你们塑造了泰德和罗宾这对备受喜爱的荧幕情侣，

690
00:30:16.980 --> 00:30:19.680
where it's always clearly hanging in the air.
他们之间的情愫总是显而易见地悬而未决。

691
00:30:19.680 --> 00:30:24.920
It's the Sam and Diane of it's the Ross and Rachel of sort of what's hanging over this show.
这简直就是本剧挥之不去的山姆与黛安、罗斯与瑞秋式的纠葛。

692
00:30:25.540 --> 00:30:32.280
And then to bring someone else into it, you are, you're, I don't want to say digging yourself into a hole,
然后把另一个人拉进来，你们，你们，我不想说这是作茧自缚，

693
00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:37.560
but you are, you're carving a path that is on, on, on, you cannot uncarve.
但你们确实在开辟一条，一旦开辟就无法回头的路。

694
00:30:37.760 --> 00:30:37.880
Yeah.
是的。

695
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:41.960
And what was the decision-making process like of, should we do this?
当时决定这么做的时候，决策过程是怎样的？

696
00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:44.020
I think we, yeah, it's a good question.
我觉得，对，这是个好问题。

697
00:30:44.080 --> 00:30:50.240
And we debated it because we were like, are we, are we burning fuel too fast on this mission in space?
我们当时讨论过，因为我们在想，我们是不是在这个太空任务中把燃料烧得太快了？

698
00:30:50.240 --> 00:30:50.500
Right.
对。

699
00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:53.200
You're always asking yourself, are we burning fuel too fast?
你总是会问自己，我们是不是燃料消耗得太快了？

700
00:30:53.280 --> 00:30:56.160
Is this a season five idea instead of a season three idea?
这到底是第五季的点子，还是第三季的点子？

701
00:30:56.380 --> 00:30:57.420
I will say this.
我得这么说。

702
00:30:57.600 --> 00:31:04.900
We had to write nine episodes in 10 and a half weeks and produce them and shoot them because of the writer's guild strike.
由于编剧工会罢工，我们不得不花十周半的时间写出九集剧本，还要把它们制作并拍完。

703
00:31:04.900 --> 00:31:14.320
Because the strike was three months and we came out of it and we had to do the most work in the shortest amount of time we ever did in the series of, you know, without,
因为罢工持续了三个月，等我们复工后，我们必须在剧集制作史上最短的时间内完成最多工作，可以说是毫无疑问的，

704
00:31:14.320 --> 00:31:15.040
without question.
毫无疑问。

705
00:31:15.040 --> 00:31:15.800
There's no debate.
这没得说。

706
00:31:15.960 --> 00:31:19.520
That was the most insane timeline of writing it to shooting it.
从写剧本到开拍，那是我们经历过最疯狂的时间表。

707
00:31:19.760 --> 00:31:24.240
And I think we, Alec, we didn't have time to worry or overthink.
我觉得我们，亚历克，我们当时根本没时间去担心或过度思考。

708
00:31:24.380 --> 00:31:30.920
We just said, maybe it is a season five idea, but we're doing it now because it's juicy and I'm excited to write it.
我们只是觉得，也许这本该是第五季的构思，但我们现在就要拍，因为它很带劲，而且我很兴奋能写这个。

709
00:31:31.080 --> 00:31:37.540
And the fact that you feel scared and you, but you can use that fear as, as fuel, as rocket fuel.
而且你内心会感到害怕，但你可以把这种恐惧当作燃料，当作火箭燃料。

710
00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:40.200
And you say, this is really scary.
然后你会说，这真的很吓人。

711
00:31:40.400 --> 00:31:41.880
This is an evil Knievel stunt.
这就像是埃弗尔·克尼弗的特技表演。

712
00:31:41.880 --> 00:31:44.440
This is, can we land on the other side of the Grand Canyon?
这就好比，我们能成功飞跃大峡谷吗？

713
00:31:44.980 --> 00:31:46.100
Let's fucking do it.
他妈的干吧。

714
00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:48.880
It's going to create so much story fallout.
这会引发无数的剧情余波。

715
00:31:48.980 --> 00:31:52.020
You're going to get episodes and episodes and episodes out of this.
接下来的好几集全都能从这衍生出来。

716
00:31:52.120 --> 00:31:55.520
You know, we, this was, what is this halfway through that back nine?
你知道的，我们，这是，这算是后半季九集的中间段吗？

717
00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:59.200
This is the fourth one in that back nine out of, we would strike hit at episode 11.
这是后半季的第四集，总共...我们是在第11集的时候遭遇罢工的。

718
00:31:59.380 --> 00:32:01.740
And then we did nine more in like 11 weeks.
然后我们在大约11周里拍完了剩下的9集。

719
00:32:02.260 --> 00:32:09.540
We, we just, we wanted to, we wanted to write something that was incredibly, that nuclear powered.
我们，我们当时就想写点威力巨大、堪称核动力一般的东西。

720
00:32:09.540 --> 00:32:12.200
We want, we wanted, we knew we were playing with something really intense.
我们，我们当时就知道我们在触碰非常强烈的东西。

721
00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:14.200
It's like the paddles that the EMT uses.
就像急救人员用的电击板一样。

722
00:32:14.380 --> 00:32:16.480
Like it, it was really, it was really, it's not a delicate tool.
就像它，真的是，它可不是个精细的工具。

723
00:32:16.920 --> 00:32:17.460
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
对，对，对。

724
00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:20.420
We, this was not a, this was not a nuanced instrument.
我们，这绝不是一个，绝不是一个讲究微妙分寸的乐器。

725
00:32:20.620 --> 00:32:22.040
This was, this was defibrillate.
这是，这直接就是电击除颤。

726
00:32:22.300 --> 00:32:23.960
Let's wake this thing up after three months.
在冰封三个月后，把这玩意儿电醒吧。

727
00:32:24.060 --> 00:32:25.840
This was, this show was on ice for three months.
